{
    "background_story": "Banks was a rising star in the electronic music scene, known for his unique ability to craft songs that resonated with listeners on a deep emotional level. His music was a masterful blend of melancholy and euphoria, often exploring the complexities of human relationships. Banks' fascination with chemistry led him to draw inspiration from the concept of valence, where atoms form bonds to achieve stability. He saw parallels between this process and the way people form connections with each other. His debut album, 'Valence', was a critically acclaimed exploration of love, loss, and the quest for balance. With each track, Banks wove a sonic tapestry that captured the intricacies of the human experience, earning him a devoted following and cementing his status as a visionary artist.",
